<article class="env-lemma" id="07QF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07QF">Lemma <span data-tag="07QF">10.166.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $A \to B$ be a smooth ring map of $k$-algebras. If $A$ is geometrically regular over $k$, then $B$ is geometrically regular over $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $k'/k$ be a finitely generated field extension. Then $A \otimes _ k k' \to B \otimes _ k k'$ is a smooth ring map (Lemma <a href="/tag/00T4" data-tag="00T4">10.137.3</a>) and $A \otimes _ k k'$ is regular. Hence $B \otimes _ k k'$ is regular by Lemma <a href="/tag/07NF" data-tag="07NF">10.163.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>